<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh 12-mth T-bill av yield rises to 15.59 pct.</title>
<headline>Kazakh 12-mth T-bill av yield rises to 15.59 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of 12-month MKM discount Treasury bills rose to 15.59 percent at an auction on July 28 from 15.35 percent at the last auction on July 14, the National Bank said.</p>
<p>Details of the auction:</p>
<p>					   July 28	    July 14</p>
<p> Series number			 KZ4CK3007986     KZ4CK1607985</p>
<p> Issue volume (million tenge)	  600		  600</p>
<p> Bids (nominal, bln tenge)	 1.2		  1.95</p>
<p> Sold (nominal, million tenge)	 600		  600</p>
<p> Average price			 86.51 pct	  86.69</p>
<p> Average yield			 15.59		15.35</p>
<p> Tenor				   364 days	   364 days</p>
<p> Maturity				July 30, 1998     July 16, 1998</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
